# Exam track — Theme: Sproochen — Sub-lesson 3: Talking About It
# @question sentences: the examiner asks in Luxembourgish, the learner
# assembles the Luxembourgish answer (always en→lu).
#
# These are the user's real answers, gathered by interview — do not "improve"
# or genericize them in a later editing pass. The point is that the learner
# rehearses what they will actually say in the Sproochentest.
#
# Question order follows the official handout: general language biography
# (mother tongue, which languages, at home, at school, the parents), then
# learning Luxembourgish, then everyday habits, then the opinion block.
#
# Key personal facts: Ukrainian native, understands Russian but prefers not to
# speak it, fluent English, basic Italian, French and Luxembourgish started;
# Ukrainian at home and with Ukrainian friends, English at work, Luxembourgish
# with the neighbours in Steinsel; learning for a bit under a year with pauses;
# online school with a teacher plus his own Duolingo-like app, flashcards and
# RTL news; wife learns with him and they will continue after the exam;
# motivation is respect for the country; Ukrainian/Luxembourgish minority-
# language parallel; hardest because there is little learning material and
# teachers are expensive; main mistakes are cases/dative and prepositions;
# favourite word Gromperekichelchen (also the hard one to pronounce, and close
# to a Ukrainian dish eaten with sour cream instead of apple jam).
#
# The @fill blocks carry frames that recur across any topic: well-causal,
# wann-conditional, obwuel-contrast, léiwer-wéi comparative, fir…ze purpose,
# dofir inversion, wärenddeems-temporal, säit-duration, a frequency adverb, a
# number, a past participle, and an Ech-mengen hedge.

@lesson L1.03 "Talking About Languages"

@word d'Fro = the question
@word d'Äntwert = the answer
@word d'Diskussioun = the discussion
@word d'Gespréich = the conversation
@word d'Theema = the topic
@word d'Meenung = the opinion
@word de Virdeel = the advantage
@word den Nodeel = the disadvantage
@word d'Integratioun = the integration
@word de Bierger = the citizen
@word d'Zukunft = the future
@word d'Land = the country
@word de Grond = the reason
@word d'Sécherheet = the confidence
@word d'Firma = the company
@word de Beruff = the profession
@word d'Stad = the city
@word d'Gemeng = the commune
@word d'Leit = the people
@word d'Kand = the child
@word d'Stonn = the hour
@word d'Middegkeet = the tiredness
@word d'Material = the material
@word den Internet = the Internet
@word d'Televisioun = the television
@word de Radio = the radio
@word den Zeitungsartikel = the newspaper article
@word d'Reklamm = the advertisement
@word d'Iddi = the idea
@word roden = to advise
@word bäibréngen = to teach
@word studéieren = to study
@word wunnen = to live
@word schaffen = to work
@word brauchen = to need
@word hëllefen = to help
@word veränneren = to change
@word integréieren = to integrate
@word offiziell = official
@word international = international
@word geléiert = qualified
@word midd = tired
@word schued = a pity
@word absolut = absolutely

# --- The general opening: languages, home, school, parents ---

@sentence
@question Firwat hutt Dir dat Theema gewielt?
@lu Ech hunn dat Theema gewielt, well Sprooche mäi Liblingstheema sinn.
@distractor-lu Aarbecht
@distractor-lu langweileg
@en I chose that topic because languages are my favourite topic.
@distractor-en work
@distractor-en boring

@sentence
@question Wat ass Är Mammesprooch?
@lu Meng Mammesprooch ass Ukrainesch.
@distractor-lu Russesch
@distractor-lu Dialekt
@en My mother tongue is Ukrainian.
@distractor-en Russian
@distractor-en dialect

@sentence
@question Wéi vill Sprooche schwätzt Dir? Wéi eng?
@lu Ech schwätzen Ukrainesch an Englesch gutt, an ech léiere Franséisch a Lëtzebuergesch.
@distractor-lu Italieenesch
@distractor-lu ni
@en I speak Ukrainian and English well, and I am learning French and Luxembourgish.
@distractor-en Italian
@distractor-en never

@sentence
@question Versteet Dir och Russesch?
@lu Russesch verstinn ech, mee ech schwätzen et léiwer net.
@distractor-lu Franséisch
@distractor-lu gär
@en I understand Russian, but I prefer not to speak it.
@distractor-en French
@distractor-en gladly

@sentence
@question Kënnt Dir Italieenesch?
@lu Mäin Italieenesch ass ganz einfach, ech kann just e puer Sätze soen.
@distractor-lu fléissend
@distractor-lu Grammatik
@en My Italian is very basic, I can say only a few sentences.
@distractor-en fluent
@distractor-en grammar

@sentence
@question Wat fir eng Sprooch schwätzt Dir doheem?
@lu Doheem schwätze mir Ukrainesch.
@distractor-lu Englesch
@distractor-lu Aarbecht
@en At home we speak Ukrainian.
@distractor-en English
@distractor-en work

@sentence
@question Wéi eng Sprooch schwätzt Dir mat Ärer Fra a mat Äre Frënn?
@lu Mat menger Fra a mat eise ukrainesche Frënn schwätzen ech Ukrainesch.
@distractor-lu Englesch
@distractor-lu Noperen
@en With my wife and with our Ukrainian friends I speak Ukrainian.
@distractor-en English
@distractor-en neighbours

@sentence
@question Wéi eng Sprooch schwätzt Dir op der Aarbecht?
@lu Op der Aarbecht schwätze mir Englesch, well meng Firma international ass.
@distractor-lu Lëtzebuergesch
@distractor-lu kleng
@en At work we speak English because my company is international.
@distractor-en Luxembourgish
@distractor-en small

@sentence
@question Mat wiem schwätzt Dir Lëtzebuergesch?
@lu Mat de Noperen a mat de Leit an der Gemeng probéieren ech Lëtzebuergesch.
@distractor-lu Kolleegen
@distractor-lu ni
@en With the neighbours and with the people in the commune I try Luxembourgish.
@distractor-en colleagues
@distractor-en never

@sentence
@question Wéi eng Sproochen hutt Dir an der Schoul geléiert?
@lu An der Schoul hunn ech Ukrainesch, Russesch an Englesch geléiert.
@distractor-lu Franséisch
@distractor-lu Universitéit
@en At school I learned Ukrainian, Russian and English.
@distractor-en French
@distractor-en university

@sentence
@question Wéi eng Sprooch hätt Dir gär op der Uni studéiert?
@lu Ech hätt gär Franséisch op der Universitéit studéiert, mee ech hunn Informatik gewielt.
@distractor-lu Russesch
@distractor-lu Schoul
@en I would have liked to study French at university, but I chose computer science.
@distractor-en Russian
@distractor-en school

@sentence
@question Wéi eng Sprooch hunn Är Eltere doheem geschwat?
@lu Meng Eltere hu Russesch geschwat, mee mat der Zäit hu si op Ukrainesch gewiesselt.
@distractor-lu Englesch
@distractor-lu ni
@en My parents spoke Russian, but over time they switched to Ukrainian.
@distractor-en English
@distractor-en never

# --- Learning Luxembourgish ---

@sentence
@question Säit wéini léiert Dir Lëtzebuergesch?
@lu Ech léiere Lëtzebuergesch säit bal engem Joer, mee mat Pausen.
@distractor-lu Woch
@distractor-lu ëmmer
@en I have been learning Luxembourgish for almost a year, but with pauses.
@distractor-en week
@distractor-en always

@sentence
@question Wat motivéiert Iech fir Lëtzebuergesch ze léieren?
@lu Fir mech ass Lëtzebuergesch e Zeeche vu Respekt fir d'Land an d'Kultur, wou mir wunnen.
@distractor-lu Aarbecht
@distractor-lu Angscht
@en For me Luxembourgish is a sign of respect for the country and the culture where we live.
@distractor-en work
@distractor-en fear

@sentence
@question Gëtt et nach aner Leit an Ärem Ëmfeld, déi Lëtzebuergesch léieren?
@lu Meng Fra léiert zesumme mat mir, an dofir üben ech doheem.
@distractor-lu eleng
@distractor-lu Kolleeg
@en My wife learns together with me, and that is why I practise at home.
@distractor-en alone
@distractor-en colleague

@sentence
@question Gitt Dir nervös wann Dir eng nei Sprooch schwätzt? Firwat?
@lu Ech gi bëssen nervös, well ech Angscht hu Feeler ze maachen.
@distractor-lu roueg
@distractor-lu Sécherheet
@en I get a little nervous because I am afraid of making mistakes.
@distractor-en calm
@distractor-en confidence

@sentence
@question Wéi hutt Dir Lëtzebuergesch geléiert?
@lu Ech léiere mat enger Léierin an engem Onlinecours a mat menger eegener App.
@distractor-lu Schoul
@distractor-lu eleng
@en I learn with a teacher in an online course and with my own app.
@distractor-en school
@distractor-en alone

@sentence
@question Bleift Dir no dem Sproochentest weider am Cours?
@lu Meng Fra an ech bleiwen no dem Sproochentest weider am Cours.
@distractor-lu ophalen
@distractor-lu Pause
@en My wife and I stay in the course after the language test.
@distractor-en stop
@distractor-en pause

@sentence
@question War et schwéier Lëtzebuergesch ze léieren, am Verglach mat anere Sproochen?
@lu Lëtzebuergesch war méi schwéier, well et wéineg Material gëtt an d'Léierinnen deier sinn.
@distractor-lu einfach
@distractor-lu bëlleg
@en Luxembourgish was more difficult because there is little material and the teachers are expensive.
@distractor-en easy
@distractor-en cheap

@sentence
@question Wat ass déi schwieregst Sprooch, déi Dir jeemools geléiert hutt? Firwat?
@lu Déi schwieregst Sprooch ass Lëtzebuergesch, well ech net vill gutt Bicher an Appe fannen.
@distractor-lu Englesch
@distractor-lu einfach
@en The most difficult language is Luxembourgish because I do not find many good books and apps.
@distractor-en English
@distractor-en easy

@sentence
@question Léiert Dir gär nei Sproochen? Wéi eng wëllt Dir fir d'nächst léieren?
@lu Ech léiere gär Sproochen, an no Lëtzebuergesch wëll ech mäi Franséisch verbesseren.
@distractor-lu Russesch
@distractor-lu vergiessen
@en I like learning languages, and after Luxembourgish I want to improve my French.
@distractor-en Russian
@distractor-en forget

# --- Everyday habits ---

@sentence
@question Wéi léiert Dir Lëtzebuergesch am Alldag?
@lu All Dag investéieren ech op d'mannst fofzéng Minutten, meeschtens moies mat menger App.
@distractor-lu Stonnen
@distractor-lu seelen
@en Every day I invest at least fifteen minutes, mostly in the morning with my app.
@distractor-en hours
@distractor-en rarely

@sentence
@question Benotzt Dir Appen oder Onlinecoursen? Wéi hëllefräich fannt Dir dat?
@lu Ech hunn eng eege App geschriwwen, an ech fanne se méi hëllefräich wéi eng grouss App.
@distractor-lu Zeitung
@distractor-lu langweileg
@en I wrote my own app, and I find it more helpful than a big app.
@distractor-en newspaper
@distractor-en boring

@sentence
@question Benotzt Dir och Karteikaarten?
@lu Heiansdo benotzen ech Karteikaarten, wann ech nei Vokabele widderhuelen.
@distractor-lu ëmmer
@distractor-lu Grammatik
@en Sometimes I use index cards when I review new vocables.
@distractor-en always
@distractor-en grammar

@sentence
@question A wat fir enger Sprooch kuckt oder liest Dir d'Noriichten?
@lu Ech liesen d'Noriichten op Englesch an op Ukrainesch, a probéiere RTL op Lëtzebuergesch.
@distractor-lu Franséisch
@distractor-lu ni
@en I read the news in English and in Ukrainian, and I try RTL in Luxembourgish.
@distractor-en French
@distractor-en never

@sentence
@question Kuckt Dir gär Filmer an der Originalversioun oder mat Ënnertitelen? Firwat?
@lu Ech kucke Filmer an der Originalversioun mat Ënnertitelen, well ech da méi verstinn.
@distractor-lu ouni
@distractor-lu manner
@en I watch films in the original version with subtitles because I then understand more.
@distractor-en without
@distractor-en less

@sentence
@question Wat maacht Dir, wann Dir eppes op Lëtzebuergesch net verstitt?
@lu Ech froen d'Persoun lues a nach eng Kéier ze schwätzen, an ech roden aus dem Kontext.
@distractor-lu séier
@distractor-lu Wierderbuch
@en I ask the person to speak slowly and once more, and I guess from the context.
@distractor-en fast
@distractor-en dictionary

@sentence
@question Wiesselt Dir dann op Englesch?
@lu Op Englesch wiesselen ech just, wann ech guer näischt méi verstinn.
@distractor-lu ëmmer
@distractor-lu Franséisch
@en I switch to English only when I no longer understand anything at all.
@distractor-en always
@distractor-en French

@sentence
@question Wat fir Feeler maacht Dir am heefegsten?
@lu Meng heefegste Feeler sinn d'Fäll, besonnesch den Dativ, an d'Prepositiounen.
@distractor-lu Aussprooch
@distractor-lu Wuertschatz
@en My most frequent mistakes are the cases, especially the dative, and the prepositions.
@distractor-en pronunciation
@distractor-en vocabulary

@sentence
@question Wéi eng Sproochen héiert Dir zu Lëtzebuerg am heefegsten?
@lu Ech héieren am heefegste Franséisch, an an de Büroe vill Englesch.
@distractor-lu Portugisesch
@distractor-lu seelen
@en I hear French most frequently, and in the offices a lot of English.
@distractor-en Portuguese
@distractor-en rarely

@sentence
@question Héiert Dir a Steinsel och Lëtzebuergesch?
@lu A Steinsel héieren ech vill Lëtzebuergesch, an dat fannen ech wonnerbar.
@distractor-lu Stad
@distractor-lu seelen
@en In Steinsel I hear a lot of Luxembourgish, and I find that wonderful.
@distractor-en city
@distractor-en rarely

@sentence
@question Wat ass Äert Liiblingswuert op Lëtzebuergesch? Firwat?
@lu Mäi Liblingswuert ass Gromperekichelchen, well et lëschteg klengt a gutt schmaacht.
@distractor-lu Sprooch
@distractor-lu langweileg
@en My favourite word is Gromperekichelchen because it sounds funny and tastes good.
@distractor-en language
@distractor-en boring

@sentence
@question Gëtt et e Wuert, wat Dir guer net ausschwätze kënnt?
@lu Gromperekichelchen ass och dat Wuert, wat ech am schwéierste soen.
@distractor-lu einfach
@distractor-lu Apel
@en Gromperekichelchen is also the word that I say with the most difficulty.
@distractor-en easy
@distractor-en apple

@sentence
@question Gëtt et dat Iessen och an Ärer Heemecht?
@lu Mir hunn en änlecht Iessen an der Ukrain, mee mir iessen et mat Sauerram.
@distractor-lu Gebeess
@distractor-lu Apel
@en We have a similar dish in Ukraine, but we eat it with sour cream.
@distractor-en jam
@distractor-en apple

# --- The opinion block ---

@sentence
@question Ass et wichteg méi Sproochen ze schwätzen? Firwat?
@lu Sprooche si wichteg, well ee sech besser integréiere kann an d'Kultur méi verstinn.
@distractor-lu onwichteg
@distractor-lu Reklamm
@en Languages are important because one can integrate better and understand the culture more.
@distractor-en unimportant
@distractor-en advertisement

@sentence
@question Wat sinn d'Virdeeler an d'Nodeeler dovun, méi Sproochen ze kënnen?
@lu De gréisste Virdeel ass d'Kommunikatioun, an den eenzege Nodeel ass déi vill Zäit.
@distractor-lu Middegkeet
@distractor-lu Angscht
@en The biggest advantage is the communication, and the only disadvantage is the amount of time.
@distractor-en tiredness
@distractor-en fear

@sentence
@question Firwat ass et wichteg Lëtzebuergesch zu Lëtzebuerg ze léieren?
@lu Ouni Lëtzebuergesch bleift ee bësse Gaascht, an ech wëll hei kee Gaascht sinn.
@distractor-lu Bierger
@distractor-lu Aarbecht
@en Without Luxembourgish one remains a bit of a guest, and I do not want to be a guest here.
@distractor-en citizen
@distractor-en work

@sentence
@question Wat haalt Dir dovun, datt Lëtzebuerg dräi offiziell Sproochen huet?
@lu Dräi offiziell Sprooche si praktesch, mee sou ass et och einfach Lëtzebuergesch ze evitéieren.
@distractor-lu schwéier
@distractor-lu Dialekt
@en Three official languages are practical, but that way it is also easy to avoid Luxembourgish.
@distractor-en difficult
@distractor-en dialect

@sentence
@question Gleeft Dir, datt jidderee Lëtzebuergesch schwätze soll, deen hei wunnt?
@lu Ech mengen, jidderee soll et op d'mannst probéieren, well et ëm Respekt geet.
@distractor-lu keen
@distractor-lu Reklamm
@en I think everybody should at least try, because it is about respect.
@distractor-en nobody
@distractor-en advertisement

@sentence
@question Ass et néideg Lëtzebuergesch op der Aarbecht ze schwätzen? Firwat?
@lu An der Informatik ass et net néideg, well eis Firmen Englesch benotzen, an dat ass schued.
@distractor-lu Bank
@distractor-lu gutt
@en In IT it is not necessary because our companies use English, and that is a pity.
@distractor-en bank
@distractor-en good

@sentence
@question Wéi eng Sprooch ass Ärer Meenung no am wichtegsten zu Lëtzebuerg? Firwat?
@lu Fir d'Aarbecht ass Englesch am wichtegsten, mee fir d'Land ass Lëtzebuergesch am wichtegsten.
@distractor-lu Russesch
@distractor-lu onwichteg
@en For work English is the most important, but for the country Luxembourgish is the most important.
@distractor-en Russian
@distractor-en unimportant

@sentence
@question Gleeft Dir, datt d'Lëtzebuerger Sprooch an Zukunft méi oder manner geschwat gëtt?
@lu Ech gleewen, si gëtt méi geschwat, well ëmmer méi Leit de Sproochentest maachen.
@distractor-lu manner
@distractor-lu Reklamm
@en I believe it is spoken more because more and more people take the language test.
@distractor-en less
@distractor-en advertisement

@sentence
@question Ass d'Positioun vum Lëtzebuergesche wéi bei enger anerer Sprooch?
@lu Ukrainesch an der Ukrain hat déiselwecht Positioun wéi Lëtzebuergesch hei.
@distractor-lu Englesch
@distractor-lu Dialekt
@en Ukrainian in Ukraine had the same position as Luxembourgish here.
@distractor-en English
@distractor-en dialect

@sentence
@question Firwat léieren d'Leit d'Sprooch vum Land net?
@lu Et ass einfach d'Sprooch vum groussen Noper ze benotzen, an dofir léiere vill Leit d'kleng Sprooch net.
@distractor-lu schwéier
@distractor-lu Kand
@en It is easy to use the language of the big neighbour, and that is why many people do not learn the small language.
@distractor-en difficult
@distractor-en child

@sentence
@question Mengt Dir, datt et méi einfach ass, eng Sprooch als Kand oder als Erwuessenen ze léieren?
@lu Als Kand ass et méi einfach, mee net wéinst dem Kapp: e Kand huet méi Zäit a manner Middegkeet.
@distractor-lu Erwuessenen
@distractor-lu Grammatik
@en As a child it is easier, but not because of the brain: a child has more time and less tiredness.
@distractor-en adult
@distractor-en grammar

@sentence
@question Verännert sech Äre Charakter, wann Dir an enger anerer Sprooch schwätzt?
@lu Et gëtt eng Theorie, datt d'Sprooch d'Denken verännert, an ech mengen, dat ass wouer.
@distractor-lu Aussprooch
@distractor-lu falsch
@en There is a theory that language changes thinking, and I think that is true.
@distractor-en pronunciation
@distractor-en wrong

@sentence
@question Wat bedeit et fir Iech, eng Sprooch wierklech fléissend ze schwätzen?
@lu Fléissend heescht fir mech, iwwer all Theema ze schwätzen ouni lang no engem Wuert ze sichen.
@distractor-lu séier
@distractor-lu Grammatik
@en Fluent means for me to speak about any topic without searching long for a word.
@distractor-en fast
@distractor-en grammar

@sentence
@question Wat géift Dir engem roden, deen ugefaang huet Lëtzebuergesch ze léieren?
@lu Sidd net faul: léiert all Dag fofzéng Minutten, well d'Widderhuelung méi wichteg ass wéi d'Talent.
@distractor-lu Woch
@distractor-lu Gléck
@en Do not be lazy: learn fifteen minutes every day, because the repetition is more important than the talent.
@distractor-en week
@distractor-en luck

@sentence
@question Soll Lëtzebuergesch als Haaptsprooch an de Schoule bäibruecht ginn? Firwat?
@lu Lëtzebuergesch soll absolut d'Haaptsprooch an de Schoule sinn, well d'Kanner d'Land da besser verstinn.
@distractor-lu Franséisch
@distractor-lu manner
@en Luxembourgish should absolutely be the main language in the schools, because the children then understand the country better.
@distractor-en French
@distractor-en less

